# PROVENANCE LAW — Athanor / Ahmes curriculum evidence

This is the controlling rule for every CD I / CD II forge run.

## Three layers (not contradictory)

| Layer | What it looks like | Where it lives | Can students see it? |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **1 · Profield routing** | `[ESTABLISHED]` / `[EMERGING]` bullets in `~/src/profield/runs/…` | pass artefacts + `03-temario-critica/C1–C3` | **Yes — verbatim when pass-audited** (excellent summaries); route in comments too |
| **2 · PROVENANCE_LINE** | One machine-readable record per **public claim** | switch-gated `curriculum-internal` comment | **No** |
| **3 · Public lesson** | Chicago `(Author Year[, page])` + **References / Referencias** | lesson body + final bibliography section | **Yes** |

Use Profield to **route** and to **draft** layer 3 prose. Layer 2 records whether Ahmes has verified the
claim (`VERIFIED`) or ingest is still blocked (`[BIBLIO-GAP]`). **References are built from layer 2**
metadata — every `public_citation` in the lesson must have a matching Chicago entry at the end.

### `[BIBLIO-GAP]` workflow (mandatory before keeping a gap)

1. Check `digital-creativity-pedagogy/grounding/gap-fields/PENDING-procurement.md` for the DOI/ISBN.
2. If a PDF exists locally, run `ahmes ingest` → `ahmes enrich --meta [--online]` → `ahmes query --cite`.
3. If procurement is `no_oa` or missing, record the attempt in `PROVENANCE_LINE` (`resolver=OMITTED;
   ahmes_attempt=<reason>`) and keep `status=[BIBLIO-GAP]` — **public prose and References may still
   cite the profield-grounded bibliography**; the gap is *vault verification*, not *silence*.
4. Never upgrade to `VERIFIED` without `evaluator_safe=yes`.

### Critical layer (layer 1½)

Temario crítica `C1-fashion-digital-world`, `C2-fashion-virtuality`, `C3-gender-minorities-silences`
supply the **critical perspective** block in every unit. Route in `CRITICAL_ROUTING:` comments; use
pass-audited `[ESTABLISHED]` sentences verbatim in public `## Critical perspective` where they fit the
unit. Map: `forge/PROFIELD-CRITICAL-MAP.md`.

The orchestrator step “write a PROVENANCE_LINE beside every claim” does **not** forbid Profield prose
in the lesson — it requires a trace for every citation that reaches students.

## The law

Every piece of Athanor discovery data and every Ahmes-derived claim must be
traceable in a source comment with one complete `PROVENANCE_LINE`. No claim is
promoted into a lesson, session prompt, assessment, media brief, or track row
without that line. A missing, partial, guessed, or vector-only trace is a
forge failure.

Athanor is discovery only. Ahmes is the citable evidence layer. A vector
preview, search result, title, or similarity score is never evidence by itself.

## Canonical record

Place this record immediately beside the claim it governs. It is one complete
provenance record, even when wrapped for readability:

```text
PROVENANCE_LINE: claim=<stable-unit.claim-id>; status=VERIFIED|[BIBLIO-GAP]|NONE; discovery={service=Athanor; project_slug=profield-digital-creativity; knowledge_scope=field_prospection; query="<exact query>"; source_locator="<exact locator>"; similarity=<number-or-null>; proposed_use="<bounded use>"}; source={document_coat="<source hash or coat>"; extraction_db="<repo-relative Ahmes extraction.db path>"; node_id="<full Ahmes node UUID>"; page_index=<zero-based-or-null>; printed_page=<page-or-null>}; resolver="<complete ahmes query --cite output, including evaluator_safe>"; quote="<short exact quote or none>"; public_citation="(<Author Year, page>) or OMITTED"; supports="<what the source supports>"; does_not_support="<transfer boundary>"
```

`[BIBLIO-GAP]` and `NONE` are honest outcomes, not invitations to invent a
source. They must include the attempted query, reason for the gap, boundary,
and `public_citation="OMITTED"`. An `evaluator_safe=no` result stays private.

In lesson Markdown, keep the full record inside the existing switch-gated
comment so internal metadata cannot reach student HTML:

```liquid
{% if site.publication.publish_internal_metadata %}
<!-- curriculum-internal:
PROVENANCE_LINE: ...
-->
{% endif %}
```

Forge-only documents under this research home may show the same comment
without Liquid gating, but must retain the exact fields. Public prose may use
only ordinary Chicago author-date citations and a complete References /
Referencias entry. Never expose Athanor, Ahmes, DevIAC, node IDs, extraction
paths, resolver output, or internal status labels (`[BIBLIO-GAP]`, `NONE`, `VERIFIED`)
in student-facing HTML. Use plain language for gaps in public prose; keep status tokens
only inside switch-gated comments.

**Board navigation.** DOI and other `http(s)` URLs that appear in public
References / Referencias must be HTML anchors with
`target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"` (never bare text). Professors open
articles on the projected lesson without leaving the page. See
`dc-unit-forge.mdc` §2 “Reference URLs (classroom board)”.

## Required gates

1. Every evidence-bearing sentence or media-research decision has a stable
   claim ID and a complete line.
2. `VERIFIED` requires the full Ahmes node, page, complete cite resolver output,
   and `evaluator_safe=yes`.
3. Every line states what the source does not support; do not infer software
   pedagogy, classroom outcomes, legal permission, or sustainability effects.
4. Internal records are switch-gated and public output has no metadata leaks.
5. Any missing line, unsafe resolver, invented quote, or rights uncertainty
   blocks promotion and is recorded as `BLOCKED`, `[BIBLIO-GAP]`, or `NONE`.

Media assets additionally require a `MEDIA_RIGHTS_LINE` from
`PROFIELD-MEDIA-PROSPECTOR-REQUEST.md`; research provenance never substitutes
for a licence record.

The whole-course controller is
`DC-CURRICULUM-ORCHESTRATOR.execute.md`.
